<title>USA: US probe of Korea, Taiwan SRAM chips to continue.</title>
<headline>US probe of Korea, Taiwan SRAM chips to continue.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A probe of certain types of memory chips imported from Korea and Taiwan will continue following a finding Friday by the U.S. International Trade Commission.</p>
<p>The ITC said it found there was a reasonable indication that U.S. industry was hurt by the imports of static random access memory semiconductors at what domestic manufacturer Micron Technology Inc had alleged was less than fair value.</p>
<p>The ITC finding means the Department of Commerce will continue its investigation of the chips with a preliminary determination due by August 4, 1997.</p>
<p>U.S. consumption of this type of memory chip totalled $1.2 billion in 1996 with $357 million worth coming from Korea and Taiwan.</p>
